Sprint 12 — Notifications

This sprint builds the internal event-driven communication engine. State changes in the system (e.g. an Admin approving a payment) will emit internal events that generate persisted notifications for Members.

IKM-12.1 — Event Emitter & Notifications Schema

Goal

Establish the foundational schema and event-bus pattern for internal decoupling.

Description

Create the notifications table and configure NestJS @nestjs/event-emitter. Define the standard payload interfaces for core domain events (e.g., PaymentApprovedEvent).

Requirements + Why

RequirementWhy it's required



notifications migration

Need a persistent store for in-app alerts so users see them upon logging in, regardless of email delivery.

@nestjs/event-emitter

Decouples the Admin controllers (e.g., ContributionController) from the Notification logic. Admin controllers shouldn't block waiting for emails to send.

Schema definition

id: uuid PK

user_id: uuid FK -> users(id)

type: varchar (e.g. PAYMENT_APPROVED, PENALTY_GENERATED)

title: varchar

message: text

is_read: boolean default false

created_at: timestamptz

Acceptance Criteria

 notifications table created.

 Event emitter module registered in MainModule.

 Core services (Contributions, Penalties) updated to emit events via this.eventEmitter.emit() instead of directly calling notification logic.

IKM-12.2 — Notification Endpoints & Handlers

User Story

As a Member, I want to see a list of my alerts and mark them as read, so I am always aware of my standing and recent payment approvals.

API Endpoints

GET /api/v1/notifications/me

PATCH /api/v1/notifications/me/:id/read

Request & Responses

GET /notifications/me

Supports ?unreadOnly=true pagination.

Returns 200 OK with an array of notification objects.

PATCH /notifications/me/:id/read

Returns 200 OK.

Authorization

@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard). Available to both MEMBER and ADMIN (though primarily used by members). A user can only fetch and mark their own notifications as read.

Internal Event Handlers

Create a NotificationListener service equipped with @OnEvent() decorators:

payment.approved: Creates a notification for the member.

penalty.generated: Creates a notification for the member.

Bonus: Uses console.log('Mock Email sent to:', user.email) to simulate external email integration.

Acceptance Criteria

 GET endpoint accurately returns the authenticated user's notifications.

 PATCH endpoint safely marks the notification as read.

 PATCH returns 404 if the notification doesn't exist or belongs to another user.

 Admin actions (approving a payment) successfully trigger the asynchronous creation of a notification row.
